    "title": "What channel is USA vs Venezuela on in WBC championship game tonight?",
    "text": "Updated March 17, 2026, 4:58 p.m. CTA champion of the World Baseball Classic is set to be crowned.Backed by two star-studded rosters, it’s Team USA vs. Venezuela in the 2026 WBC final at loanDepot Park in Miami. First pitch is set for 7 p.m. Central time.The final, airing on Fox, will conclude a thrilling tournament that started with 20 teams showcasing baseball’s global game.USA, which defeated Dominican Republic in the semifinals, is looking to win its second WBC after capturing the 2017 championship. It fell short in 2023, losing to Japan in the final.Venezuela knocked out the Shohei Otani-led Japan team in the quarterfinals of this year’s tournament and then rallied to defeat Italy in the semifinals.Venezuela is seeking its first WBC title.Milwaukee Brewers fans will likely be tuning in. Four players from the team will take the field in the final. Brice Turang has been one of the top players for Team USA, while Jackson Chourio, William Contreras and Angel Zerpa are key players for Venezuela.Here’s what to know about the WBC championship, including start time and where to watch:What time is the World Baseball Classic today? Team USA vs Venezuela start timeTime: 7 p.m. CTDate: Tuesday, March 17The World Baseball Classic championship game between Team USA and Venezuela is at 7 p.m. Tuesday, March 17 at loanDepot Park in Miami.Team USA baseball vs Venezuela TV, live stream: World Baseball Classic where to watchTV: Fox (Channel 6 in Milwaukee)Live stream: Fubo (free trial) and the ESPN+ Fox One BundleStream the WBC on FuboTeam USA World Baseball Classic rosterThe team is a collection of All-Stars, MVPs, batting champs, home run champs and World Series heroes.Players include the likes of Aaron Judge (New York Yankees), Bryce Harper (Philadelphia Phillies), Kyle Schwarber (Philadelphia Phillies), Cal Raleigh (Seattle Mariners), Will Smith (Los Angeles Dodgers), Alex Bregman (Chicago Cubs), Gunnar Henderson (Baltimore Orioles), Paul Goldschmidt (New York Yankees), Bobby Witt Jr. (Kansas City Royals), Brice Turang (Milwaukee Brewers), among others, at the plate and pitchers like Paul Skenes (Pittsburgh Pirates) and Logan Webb (San Francisco Giants).Mark DeRosa is the manager.See the full roster hereWatch with ESPN Unlimited + Fox One bundleVenezuela World Baseball Classic rosterThe Venezuela roster is also full of players who have made multiple All-Star Game appearances, won batting titles, an MVP and are World Series champions.Players include the likes of William Contreras (Milwaukee Brewers), Salvador Perez (Kansas City Royals), Luis Arraez (San Diego Padres), Maikel Garcia (Kansas City Royals), Willson Contreras, Eugenio Suarez (Cincinnati Reds), Gleyber Torres (Detroit Tigers), Ronald Acuna Jr. (Atlanta Braves) and Jackson Chourio (Milwaukee Brewers). Among the pitchers are Daniel Palencia (Chicago Cubs) and Ranger Suarez (Boston Red Sox).Former MLB player Omar Lopez, the current bench coach of the Houston Astros, is the manager. Twleve-time All-Star, four-time batting champion and two-time MVP Miguel Cabrera, who retired after the 2023 season, is a hitting coach.See the full Venezuela rosterTeam USA's WBC lineup vs VenezuelaWitt, Harper, Judge and Schwarber continue to be the top four batter's for DeRosa's lineup:Here's the full starting lineup for Team USA against Venezuela:Who is pitching for USA in final vs Venezuela?For USA, New York Mets 24-year-old rookie Nolan McLean gets the ball, while 32-year-old Eduardo Rodriguez, a 10-year MLB veteran with the Arizona Diamondbacks, starts for Venezuela.World Baseball Classic bracketTwenty teams began the tournament with pool-play games at four sites across the world. The top two teams in each group advanced to the knockout round. Now, it comes down to USA vs. Venezuela for the title.",
